  "body": "## \ud83c\udfaf Changes\n\nAdds seven Vue examples ported from the React examples, and registers them in the Vue examples section of `docs/config.json`.\n\n- `basic-graphql-request`, `default-query-function`, `devtools-panel`, `playground`, `shadow-dom`, `algolia` and `chat`\n- Each example follows the setup of `examples/vue/basic` (Vite, `vue-tsc`, `optimizeDeps.exclude`, ESLint with `flat/recommended-strict`, `flat/recommended` for `default-query-function`) and keeps the data layer in `src/services/{domain}` with query factories.\n- Vue-specific differences from the React examples:\n  - `default-query-function` sets the default `queryFn` through `VueQueryPlugin`'s `queryClientConfig`.\n  - `playground` updates the `QueryClient` defaults with `setDefaultOptions` in a `watchEffect`.\n  - `shadow-dom` mounts the app into a `div` inside the shadow root, because `mount` does not accept a `ShadowRoot`.\n  - `algolia` derives the hits with `computed` instead of `select`.\n  - `devtools-panel` uses `VueQueryDevtoolsPanel`.\n- Examples that import CSS include `src/vite-env.d.ts`.\n\n## \u2705 Checklist\n\n- [x] I have followed the steps in the [Contributing guide](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [x] I have tested code changes locally with `pnpm run test:pr`, or these tests do not apply to this pull request.\n- [x] I have followed the [AI contribution policy](https://github.com/TanStack/query/blob/main/AI_POLICY.md) and fully understand the code in this pull request, including any code generated with AI assistance.\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 Release Impact\n\n- [ ] This change affects published code, and I have generated a [changeset](https://github.com/changesets/changesets/blob/main/docs/adding-a-changeset.md).\n- [x] This change is docs/CI/dev-only (no release).\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added seven Vue examples to the navigation: GraphQL requests, default query functions, an interactive playground, Algolia search, Shadow DOM, an embedded devtools panel, and streaming chat.\n  * Examples demonstrate features such as searchable results, editable todos, post details, repository data, and incremental chat responses.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added setup and development instructions for each new example.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
